{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes","id":407873,"title":"The way you play the Pure tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-16T09:48:12-08:00","id":407873,"title":"The way you play the Pure tribes","content":"Forsaken is one of my favorite game from white wolf/onyx path along with apocalypse.<br /> By the way, If the message of WtA was (and is, actually) more direct, I strongly think that the whole metaplot of Forsaken is more phiosopical and complicated to understand.<br /> The ''sins of the fathers'', the responsabilites, the animal nature, the power of the pack, the werewolf instincts, the rage, the wolf blooded, the family, the territory, the horror, the fight,the vengeance.<br /> Vengeance. That's a ''must'' only for three tribes, and we know why.<br /> I think that the Pure tribes are one of the most intersting and complicated things of the whole new world of darkness to understand, in a psychological point of view.<br /> If the forsaken werewolves, (for the most) have to follow the example and their instincts to being part of the uratha ''society'' and protect the balance of the material/spiritual worlds for a diffrent kind of purposes, showing how they can redeem themselves from their ancestral ''sin'', the Anshega show us something else: no compromise, no surrender, only revenge and domination.<br /> The Pures have a more ''extreme'' culture based maybe more on animal behaviors than human behaviors.<br /> They are savage and wild, they are probably more united then the forsaken and they seems to be more related to the wild and hostyle places fo the world.<br /> They are the quintessence of being a werewolf, well, the <i>monster</i> we know as ''werewolf''. They do not hunt only because is in their dna, they're on the hunt for a more ''great concept'' of territory, involving revenge.<br /> I find them ''romantic'' in some way.<br /> They seems to be a symbol of ''savage beauty'' to me, some kind of last stand against the modern world, with their ferocity and immorality towards humans I like to think about them as<br /> a remain of the ancient times ( make me think about dark eras and the pure), an implacable force of nature with the most ferocious attributes of humanity and animals, far from modern concepts and technology (maybe not <i>always,</i> but for sure more than the forsaken).<br /> <br /> So, when I play WtF and we decide to play as the Anshega, It's interesting and also difficult to build the psicological backgrounds of the characters, trying to understand the ''foundamentalists'' traditions (maybe the most human things the Pures have) but also how this traditions mix up with the werewolf instincts, and <i>how </i>role all of this.<br /> So, what do you do when you play as a pure?<br /> have you ever played as one?<br /> You play also to understand why they act like they act?<br /> You play only to slash, kill, burn and hunt humans and forsaken?<br /> Do you <i>really</i> think they are the bad guys?<br /> <br /> I wish to hear some opinions here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I hope the thread is decently understandable<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 02-16-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T09:59:10-08:00","id":407905,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to know your primary language, not a slam or anything just curious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> your grammar structure makes me think it isn't english is all. <br /> <br /> The pure are to a large extent the romanticized werewolf, but also a lot of other extremes in society. That's not to say they all act like rabid animals. The fire touched are a touch rabid in the head, and have some fundamental differences from the others, but the silver fangs represent something else too. The predator kings we all know as well, and their motivations, while revenge, are for different reasons. Some hunt for the revenge of father wolf, others do not.<br /> <br /> Take for example the predator kings. They seek revenge not for the death of father wolf. In their eyes he needed to go for his weakness to fall to his children. Rather they seek revenge because the act ruined their hunters paradise. Dire wolf HATES for that reason and that reason only. Man kind is ruining his ideal world and driving it further from the truth that he knows. <br /> <br /> Guess its obvious which tribe i love eh? Personally if I play a predator king its going to be the savage hunter of the wilderness. The guy living off the grid, the extreme example of what the hunters in darkness try to be. A man who embraces his beast fully, maybe an individual who grew up loving american werewolf in london and assumes thats the werewolf norm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:12:11-08:00","id":407909,"title":"","content":"You used Silver Fangs in place of Ivory Claws, Lyrics. Not that I blame you; they follow Silver Wolf and basically are the Silver Fangs!<br /> <br /> Boiled down to their most simple components the Pure are the children who rejected their mother, if you believe the mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 02-16-2015, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:14:20-08:00","id":407919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=407905#post407905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to know your primary language, not a slam or anything just curious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> your grammar structure makes me think it isn't english is all.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>growed up in south tyrol speaking and learning german and italian in a family that only talk in venetian slang xD<br /> <br /> <br /> I really like all the pure tribes but I often choose the ivory claws or the predator kings.<br /> I like the concept of purity about the ivory claws and their role as alpha tribe ( at least, ''tactician'' pure tribe) and I love to blow up my mind thinking about a ''realistic'' predator king who hates humans and why<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T10:29:07-08:00","id":407935,"title":"","content":"I haven't played a Pure, but I did have a character that was rejected by every Forsaken totem due to constantly failing their tests. She would have been an archetypical Predator King had she not hated the Pure as much as fire hates water. There is, however, one thing I've noticed with the Pure tribes vs. the Forsaken:<br /> <br /> <b>Tradition vs. modernism, and civilization vs. the untamed.</b><br /> <br /> The Forsaken, mostly, have adapted to the ever-changing ebb and flow that humanity has brought to the planet. Despite wolfish instincts that call for pack and prey, they try to blend their own cultures with the human landscape wherever they can. On the other hand, the Pure are reminiscent of ways of thinking most of us would find medieval: in-breeding and purity of bloodline (Ivory Claws), a religious fanaticism that is treated as law (Fire-Touched), and barbaric, Darwinian ways of thinking that are brutal and unforgiving in practise (the Predator Kings). These tribes are still treating humans as if they are the frightened livestock that the werewolves herded around in Pangaea, with as little change as possible. Heck, the PKs <i>will chain up their wolf-blooded and raise them like cattle,</i> to the point where their kin are as bad-off as feral children in development and psychology.<br /> <br /> You could also argue that the Forsaken have domesticated themselves compared to the Pure. Just as humanity is accepting more ideas that fall into the category of &quot;this is NOT okay to do to other beings&quot; (murder, torture, slavery, etc.), the Forsaken are looking at each other and going, &quot;Is this really okay, guys?&quot; The Pure, on the other hand, are more likely to embrace the more &quot;savage wolf&quot; aspects of their beastly sides, and dance over human morality like it's dirt on the ground. They're half-spirit hunter-lords, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T11:22:30-08:00","id":407968,"title":"","content":"I've used several Pure in my campaign, ranging from slimy Neo-Nazis to a veritable werewolf saint, and the analogy I keep coming back to is that of religion. Essentially, the Pure and the Forsaken are two rival faiths, which have a shared core of history and belief, yet extremely different interpretations of certain elements (like the role of Luna or the practice of keeping spirits on the far side of the Gauntlet). <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">A good analogy might be that the Forsaken are Catholics, and the various Pure tribes are different flavors of Protestants, with their own, often severe differences, but at the same time united in the face of a common antagonist. Likewise, relations between Forsaken and Pure range from bloody religious war to uneasy accommodation to live-and-let-live ecumenicism. (I've also heavily de-emphasized the role of Totems and Firstborn as ideological commissars).<br /> <br /> The Pure as utter villains didn't really fly too well in my campaign since most of my players found the Pure tribes much more memorable and interesting than the Forsaken ones (which were usually seen as kind of bland), so we had a few sympathetic Pure pop up. Then after a while we stepped back, realized that we have roughly equal levels of scuminess and nobility in both Pure and Forsaken, and so we reinterpreted and tweaked the backstory into a more neutral viewpoint between the two. </span></span><br /> <br /> (You can also check via my signature some of the Tribal reimaginings done by one of my players, which include the Pure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T11:23:46-08:00","id":407970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=407935#post407935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. On the other hand, the Pure are reminiscent of ways of thinking most of us would find medieval: in-breeding and purity of bloodline (Ivory Claws), a religious fanaticism that is treated as law (Fire-Touched), and barbaric, Darwinian ways of thinking that are brutal and unforgiving in practise (the Predator Kings).</div> </div> </div> </div>PK have always been blunt in their dealings and the like but the overlap between Fire Touched and Ivory Claws at times gets somewhat confusing. ICs go on about &quot;purity&quot; but most of that seems internally focused. Fire-Touched on the other hand, are all about the external fight. Fire burns, convert or die.<br /> <br /> So it's easy to get FT and PK working in a game. Less so than the IC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T11:35:20-08:00","id":407979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=407935#post407935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tradition vs. modernism, and civilization vs. the untamed.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>A common theme in Vampire's covenants, as well. I've never played a Pure myself. The book came out well after our first game, so in our first game we played them as sort of undercover werewolves. It was a lot like Demon the Descent, actually, if you viewed the Forsaken as Angels and switched Luna for the God Machine. They just pretended to be normal, Forsaken werewolves and worked on destroying their alliances while also seeking to return the world to Pangaea.<br /> <br /> I really grew to like the Pure once the book came out, though. The Fire-Touched and Predator Kings are probably my favorites. I like the romanticized, back to the old times beliefs of the Pure but for some reason they have a hard time being seen as realistic to me, Pangaea, as it is, doesn't seem like it can come back. In our first game the Pure actually had a plan to throw an entire city into the Shadow, including having it be 'forgotten' by the rest of the world. We managed to stop the plan but as I read more and more books it just seems like something that hasn't ever happened or will happen, though it would be cool to see some samples of places like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:23:10-08:00","id":408057,"title":"","content":"Being the proud Social Justice Warrior I am, I like to imagine the Pure as a postmodernist deconstruction of the original werewolf myth-ie, Werewolf As Hostile Stranger Capable of Pretending To Not Be a Stranger.<br /> <br /> The twist is that, obviously, the Hostile Stranger in question is more like an actual stranger, which is to say, a person you don't know. He isn't a stranger everywhere, he has his own culture and friends and such. Thing is, he's still <i>hostile, </i>because his culture is so mired in xenophobia that he <i>wants </i>to be a stranger-he knows enough about your culture that he is disgusted by the idea of talking to anyone not in his social orbit. His motive? He may talk a good game about the natural order and the inhumanity of man to the planet, but really, it's because he's terrified of the world outside his little bubble; it's big, it's unfamiliar, it doesn't care for him very much because, well, it doesn't know him. Far better to withdraw, to growl, to curse and tear anyone who doesn't look like him, who doesn't sound like him.<br /> <br /> In effect, the true werewolves are the people who make werewolf myths as an excuse to hate the stranger. That they are actually werewolves is just icing on the irony cake.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean they're unsympathetic, of course; fear makes monsters out of all of us, and pretending the Pure are any different from everyone else is a good way to <i>become </i>the Pure. But the Pure are afraid, and that fear drives their savagery-because if the world is afraid of <i>them, </i>well, then it won't hurt them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T12:35:11-08:00","id":408066,"title":"","content":"I played a PK once and it was awesome and dramatic. My character was a naive pup but a critical thinker, which got him a whole lot of trouble with the tribe. He understood the tribe's philosophy but did not agree on it wholly. That's because both of his parents are human with a bit of werewolf genes in them. He did not think &quot;all&quot; humans are a disease that must be tamed or extinguish. After all, most of them came from regular humans who loved and despised them, as my character said. My character got to a point where he was so close into becoming a Forsaken, but that changed when Hunters killed his parents in searched of his pack, which snapped him and his view of humanity. I think the PK are the most interesting Pure tribe of them all. I kind of felt sympathy for them to the point where I viewed them as &quot;romantic&quot; as well. Kind of like, you were once a good man with high beliefs until humanity struck you down and destroyed the man you once were. Now you hunt them without any remorse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T13:21:54-08:00","id":408127,"title":"","content":"I've always wanted to play as an ivory claw version of myself. My screwed up real life family would be PERFECT as an Ivory Claw bloodline, since we could be described as &quot; fallen noblity&quot; (meaning my family used to be rich, but that was before I was born). My advice to anybody playing as an Ivory Claw would be to talk to your living ancestors about the skeletons in your family's closets for inspiration, since Ivory claws are all about screwed up families and their secrets, in my opinion. Your relatives may be reluctant to share, but it will be worth it. And if your grandmother (or whoever) doesn't want to talk about it, then genealogy sites can dig a bare minimum of dirt on your ancestors that you can steal ideas from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T14:06:21-08:00","id":408178,"title":"","content":"Whoops my bad on the silver fangs. I do that a lot too. I like all the pure, but not in a way that Id actively try all the tribes. Just the Kings, and only because of my previous examples. That and there's some beastiality sexyness to the primal monster. I don't think id do the other tribes justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T14:23:37-08:00","id":408190,"title":"","content":"The Pure took the easy path. Subservience to the shadowy lords of the spirit world in exchange for personal security. Literally bargained their freedom away for it. As a whole, their culture is one of Hatred, the kind which leads people to commit atrocities on par to crimes against humanity. There's nothing romantic about worshiping living flames that would love nothing more than to consume the whole world, or a huge carnivorous plant that would devour your brother and slowly digest it over weeks in your very presence, while moving around his skin, for an unknowable slight you committed against the alien being.<br /> <br /> Pure, when I portray them, are invariably horrifying, sickening beings that don't realize that they sold their souls to a devil, and it loves to watch how they chip it away, and away night after night by their own choices.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken are not above those lows, regardless. Anyone, no matter which oath they took can have a moment of weakness and indulge in the base appetites of their beastly nature. But the Pure celebrate them. Torture, rape, mass murder. Those are the things that the Pure exalt on their heroes. Those are the examples they look up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:21:13-08:00","id":408344,"title":"","content":"Your pure sound like bale hounds there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:30:46-08:00","id":408353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408344#post408344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your pure sound like bale hounds there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what I was thinking, that or the Islamic State.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:01:38-08:00","id":408473,"title":"","content":"Exactly like Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:25:13-08:00","id":408488,"title":"","content":"Portraying them as being inherently antagonistic when there's an incompatibility between their central tenants and <b>your existence</b> does not seem to be a disservice to how they're written. They have some nuances here and there, but overall they really are a culture of hatred, bitterness, and zealotry with a strong victim complex. When I portray them I like to make a couple characters that can be empathized with, but I quickly establish that they're the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:43:26-08:00","id":408521,"title":"","content":"Not saying they shouldn't be antagonists, but if his pure are so dark how the hell dark are his hounds? I mean my gods it must be a clive barker story when they get involved!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:37:40-08:00","id":408564,"title":"","content":"The difference between Bale Hounds and Pure, in my portrayal of them, is that the later group isn't secretive about their allegiance (for the most part), and would never, ever, consider inflicting the atrocities that the former group would to their own packmates (who are, in essence, their family. Dysfunctional as it may be).<br /> <br /> The Pure are ultimately misguided - they don't even realize how much they're screwing themselves up for the delusional fantasies of shadowy beings.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds know that they're damned, and they embrace that condition wholeheartedly. Pure might rip your heart out with silver knives, but Bale Hounds will bind your spirit to Wounds in eternal torment. There is death, and there are fates worse than it.<br /> <br /> A young Anshega might realize the irony, the sad hypocrisy of his condition, and shed his crimson marks for the silver ones of the Tribes of the Moon. Bale Hounds are invariably, every single one of them, beyond redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:48:17-08:00","id":408565,"title":"","content":"Can the pure even regain their silver brands? i'm pretty sure Luna rescinds any chance of redemption from the pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:51:54-08:00","id":408566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408353#post408353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's what I was thinking, that or the Islamic State.</div> </div> </div> </div>A sidebar from their book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Pure, pg 38</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrorism<br /> Some Pure rely on terrorist-style tactics as means to an end. The objective of terrorism is not direct violence \u2013 certainly that\u2019s a common result, but the goal is fear. By causing violence or by threatening the spread of mayhem, fear weakens the enemy. If taking a pack\u2019s wolf-blooded family and cutting off their hands and feet and hanging them from the locus sends a message to the Forsaken and clouds their judgment with terror and rage, then the Pure have succeeded. If setting an old-growth forest aflame helps diminish the Forsaken in some way, then that is what is necessary, no matter who or what burns along with it.<br /> Certainly, some Pure don\u2019t consider terrorism a viable tactic. In seeking to maintain some kind of honor, some Pure prefer to take the Forsaken on directly, often marching into the enemy\u2019s territory and demanding a fight. That said, most Pure have trouble seeing past the hate that drives them inexorably forward. They believe that what they do serves a greater good, and that dishonor is forgiven if done in the name of righteousness.<br /> Of course, the Pure don\u2019t think of themselves as terrorists. As with people, one man\u2019s terrorist is another man\u2019s freedom fighter.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:53:53-08:00","id":408568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408565#post408565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the pure even regain their silver brands? i'm pretty sure Luna rescinds any chance of redemption from the pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be entirely the call of the Lodge of Salvation. To redeem the Pure back. To un-brainwash them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T20:59:36-08:00","id":408572,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing with you, though I don't share your view, I'm trying to understand it better. What do you mean when you say they're 'screwing themselves up?'<br /> <br /> They definitely are taking the easy way out, of course, rather than diplomacy or trying to fulfill Luna's mandate of guardianship, they want that one big win, after which they can live like kings, or at least not confined the way they think the Forsaken are, the way they feel they deserve to.<br /> <br /> They die just like the Forsaken, though. The Bale Hounds seem to be the only ones with a chance for a semblance of life after death, with the maeladar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:03:37-08:00","id":408576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408572#post408572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They die just like the Forsaken, though. The Bale Hounds seem to be the only ones with a chance for a semblance of life after death, with the maeladar.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's Taga-Dan, mind, but that's kind of definitely unconfirmable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:06:41-08:00","id":408579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408576#post408576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Taga-Dan, mind, but that's kind of definitely unconfirmable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's right, there's probably a lodge or two with some concept of an afterlife as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:10:15-08:00","id":408581,"title":"","content":"The atrocities that the Pure revere in their heroes chip away chunks of their souls. No matter what penance they may indulge themselves in. In the end, exalted elders would suffer from maladies born from their reduced Harmony not unlike chronic diseases and dementia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:19:12-08:00","id":408585,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the Forsaken get the same derangements and issues with Harmony loss. And their job is an unending one. If tomorrow a Predator King managed to plunge the entire world into a new Pangaea, wouldn't it be worth the pain of his soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:42:29-08:00","id":408594,"title":"","content":"The point here is that one society tries to at least manage the most negative, beastly urges of their members. The other reveres it. For them &quot;A werewolf who tortures a Forsaken captive into revealing information about his pack is due Honor, but one who tortures the captive into swearing the Oath of Urfarah is due Purity.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet was the final act of Urfarah while he lived, which arose with his death-howl, without that divide the world would be overrun by spirit fiefdoms and hellish realms, not unlike what Pangaea was turning into before he had to be put down. So no. Not at all. The Pure? They would still be what they are today, in the unlikely event that they managed to tear it down: Slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:46:40-08:00","id":408596,"title":"","content":"Okay I see where you're coming from now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T21:58:06-08:00","id":408603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408344#post408344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your pure sound like bale hounds there.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they sound like the Pure as presented in the Pure sourcebook. The Pure really do all that bad shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:05:18-08:00","id":408607,"title":"","content":"When considering playing the Pure, don't forget their Totems and the crippling restrictions they give the packs they enslave. The Pure book mentions, as examples of totem bans that apply to individual Pure packs, offering their Totem children's fingers every couple days; having to fuck whenever there's a chance, having to consume human or wolf flesh once a week while still keeping their Harmony higher than 5; burning down at least one building per week, etc. Pure totem bans take away a significant part of a werewolf's freedom. That's the price the Pure pay for an existence that is safer and less plagued by moral quandaries and concerns than that of the Forsaken. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> You can't have any real peace. The entire ethos behind the Pure is that they believe they will have their redemption and victory when all of the Forsaken are converted or dead.<br /> <br /> Muslims and Christians can have peace. They worship the same god even if they kill each other over the details sometimes. But Christians and Al Qaeda will never have peace, since it's the stated goal of Al Qaeda to kill Westerners in the name of a global Islamic movement.<br /> <br /> That's the Pure. They actively believe that genocide - genocide - is a valid way for them to come out on top and achieve the way of life they want. Ironically, they're already on top. The Forsaken are the underdogs, savagely fighting for survival. The Pure are already dominant, yet they whine about being martyrs.<br /> <br /> Ugh.<br /> <br /> Look, ultimately Werewolf is about telling stories. A story needs compelling antagonists in order to make the struggles of the main characters worthwhile. Eric Draven and his crow had Top Dollar and the gang members, for example. They were not good people who got a bad rap or had excellent reasons for their actions. They were shitheads who did awful things because they wanted to, because no-one ever stopped them before. You didn't watch The Crow and think &quot;Wow, they've got it right. A film about these guys would be so much edgier and cooler.&quot; Same thing with the Pure.<br /> <br /> Yes, Werewolf is a game. But it is a game about telling stories. In this regard, people misunderstanding the Pure are not saying &quot;I want to use a blue counter instead of a red counter&quot; or &quot;I want to be the top hat instead of the battleship.&quot; They're saying &quot;I want to be the story's antagonists, like Top Dollar, or Sephiroth, or Syndrome.&quot; These are all characters designed to be fantastic antagonists because of their beliefs and their actions driving them to do evil things. That's what's cool about them.<br /> <br /> The Pure are not shallow Chaotic Evil bad guys who exist solely to kill things. But they are compelling antagonist characters in a story - and that's what they were always meant to be. They are by equal measures evil, selfish, misguided and fanatical. They do horrible things because they believe - wrongly - that they are the right things to do. And that's the key point. What they believe is essentially a lie. Their beliefs rise from a moment that their own ancestors failed to do the right thing. They compound that failure by insisting that things will be great for them again - no matter at what cost to humans - if they succeed in genocide or converting the Forsaken. The world of humans will be at the mercy of the Shadow, if that ever happened.<br /> <br /> I don't buy into the Forsaken en masse as goody-goody heroes, though that's a concept with a lot of mileage in some groups and character backgrounds. They're desperate, almost-beaten people like you and me, looking to survive in a world that hates them. Simple as that. Part of the world that hates them is the Pure, who press on their crusade with howls of martyrdom, much like the people who crashed those planes into the Twin Towers.<br /> <br /> &quot;You've wronged us!&quot; they cry. Uh, well...I haven't wronged them. Neither have you. Neither have the Forsaken. Yet we'd all pay when the Pure come to town, much like 3,000 innocent people paid when planes smashed into their buildings. The guys flying those planes had their reasons for doing it, but their reasons were fucking weak. They were wrong.<br /> <br /> The Pure and the Forsaken are not the Camarilla and Sabbat. They are not the opposite sides of the same coin, with both sides holding noble beliefs that the other side can't understand. Eric Draven's enemies were not just guys who saw things differently to him. They were malicious characters who did terrible things and that made them great antagonists. The Pure have their reasons for what they do, but their reasons are equal parts just lies and misguided excuses for horrendous acts. It's part of their tragedy and their terror. <br /> <br /> Put simply: the good guys are the ones who are taking responsibility for making the world around them a better place. The bad guys are the ones who are killing people based on the deeds of their ancestors, or at the very least forcing said people to accept their dogma. The lines are very clear here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:09:32-08:00","id":408614,"title":"","content":"With the new harmony style does it still chip away at them? It isn't on the morality scale anymore it's how balanced are you. The predator kings are likely to be unbalanced to the wolf, but the ivory claws? Guess we'll need 2e to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T03:20:11-08:00","id":408731,"title":"","content":"A lot of interesting point of view.<br /> My point is a little bit different. I agree for the most with Christian A, but I'm deeply thinking about the Harmony of the pures.<br /> Of course their methods, for a human mind are brutal and ferocious, and they sacrificed their freedom (and a lot of theyr mental sanity) for their powerful spirit allies.<br /> Play as a pure is like play as a foundamentalist of course, but we're still judging a culture that it's only half human.<br /> Like Christian A said, the pure and forsaken are not like camarilla and sabbat or black spiral and garou.<br /> In facts, they kills each other with passion when they can, but the fight between pure and forsaken seems to be more a dominance fight, than always a fight till death, like pack of wolves.<br /> Killing another werewolf is a very dangerous matter, for your harmony, for the feuds you can generate, for the retaliation that you must wait in return.<br /> Like explained on War Against the Pure, often is the large scale war that break out with a lot of dead werewolves.<br /> When I portray the pure I often show them like some kind of primordial, brainwashed sect of dangerous criminals organized in pack, striking more to show their dominance and their ''reason'' above the forsaken mission. For the Fire touched I prefer also the social war, making situation where the pure seems to have all the reasons from their part, portraying them like ''good samaritans'' during a moment of weakness of a player.<br /> For the Ivory Claws I prefer the psychological warfare. Like a pack of wolves who surround you, hiding in the woods starting howling to seems more than they are in numbers. The Ivory claws works well also to show some of the most brutal traditions to keep themselves (and others) purest among the pure. I tried a lot to made them acts with the <u><i>best</i></u> ''animal morality'' along with the <u><i>wrost </i></u>''human morality''.<br /> And the Predator Kings, I prefer to show how much they don't give a fuck for the most. In a culture of hatred theyr foundamentalist behaviors seems colllapsed in the name of their ''freedom''. They grow up among the wildest of the werewolf tribes purging away human concepts and morality, not everyone, but a lot of them are simply free to act like animals, just because they totally brainwashed their kin from millenia. They are the monstrous werewolves, eaters of human flash, hunters among the hunters, they fight a war maybe just because the forsaken seems to be weak at their eyes, or just because... they like it, for matters intrinsic of their culture.<br /> In other words, yes the pures seems to be already dominat ( probably they are) but I think they feel desperate too, convinced about the superiority fo their culture and religious view they watch the world and they know, that the only things dominant are the human race, something disgusting for them, they are the ultimate hunters and they are forced to hide and watch how their ''brothers'' (forsaken) deal with humanity and spirits embracing Luna as their patron after a patricide?. But none of them can admit it, so, once you embraced your animal instinct you can just do two things: fight or <i>Tagadan.</i><br /> Pride and zeal above logic and surrender.<br /> The spirits prove that the reasons of the pure are right, after all.<br /> <br /> But the forsaken prove their strenght too, who play will see","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 02-17-2015, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T04:55:31-08:00","id":408793,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the Pure far too much as antagonists to the Forsaken for my games to ever run a chronicle wherein the player characters are Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T09:40:10-08:00","id":409055,"title":"","content":"I portray the pure as the hunters that couldn't adapt. The predator kings in particular spend so Much time mourning for Pangaea, rather than adapting to their current environment. I run Pure as sympathetic villains. You can see why they think the way they do, and you can see what they experienced to make them the way they are, but that in no way actually justifies their behavior or excuses them from the crimes they commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T00:05:18-08:00","id":409764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408731#post408731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Fire touched I prefer also the social war, making situation where the pure seems to have all the reasons from their part, portraying them like ''good samaritans'' during a moment of weakness of a player.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key to portraying the Fire-Touched the right way, in my opinion, is to remember that they show only their best, most appealing and seductive side when dealing with the Forsaken. At first. They're very good at what they do, and they really believe in the shit they're selling.<br /> <br /> And why wouldn't you want to join them? It's the winner's side. They get to have strength in numbers. They get to have the most powerful spirit allies (what must it be like, you wonder - not to be afraid of spirits anymore? Not to be scared for your life every single time you enter the Shadow? Not to have the threat of being jumped by freak shadow beings and Ridden hanging over you all the time?). And then there's the freedom granted to them by their dogma that the Forsaken can never have - running wild and free, hunting and killing as you like, never looking back at the consequences. <br /> <br /> You don't get to see the downsides until you're thoroughly hooked and can't go back. <br /> <br /> To any young, inexperienced wolf (read: the PCs, usually), the Fire-Touched and what little they see and know about their beliefs should, by all means, be tempting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408731#post408731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Predator Kings, I prefer to show how much they don't give a fuck for the most. In a culture of hatred theyr foundamentalist behaviors seems colllapsed in the name of their ''freedom''. They grow up among the wildest of the werewolf tribes purging away human concepts and morality, not everyone, but a lot of them are simply free to act like animals, just because they totally brainwashed their kin from millenia. They are the monstrous werewolves, eaters of human flash, hunters among the hunters, they fight a war maybe just because the forsaken seems to be weak at their eyes, or just because... they like it, for matters intrinsic of their culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy showing my players very little of the Ninna Farakh motivations and beliefs - I prefer letting the Fire Touched act as advocates for the Pure. The Predator Kings, in my games, don't ever come to talk. The Pure are supposed to be to the Forsaken what movie werewolves are to regular movie humans, as the Predators book puts it, yes? The Predator Kings exemplify that fact. They make fantastic antagonists because they can't be reasoned with; they're the things out there in the woods that you don't see until it's too late. You start to retreat, they start to pursue. You begin to run; more shadows join in, howling, pouncing, tiring you out until it's time to end it all. They only ever come for one reason - to hunt, with you being their prey. <br /> <br /> They're more wolf-monsters than men. I usually don't show them in human form in my games. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408731#post408731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, yes the pures seems to be already dominat ( probably they are) but I think they feel desperate too, convinced about the superiority fo their culture and religious view they watch the world and they know, that the only things dominant are the human race, something disgusting for them, they are the ultimate hunters and they are forced to hide and watch how their ''brothers'' (forsaken) deal with humanity and spirits embracing Luna as their patron after a patricide?. But none of them can admit it, so, once you embraced your animal instinct you can just do two things: fight or <i>Tagadan.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember, also, that the Pure truly believe themselves to be victims of a cosmic struggle that started an apocalypse ago. They whine about being martyrs for a holy cause, they think they're the underdogs of the setting who've been wronged more than anyone else - yet they have all the numbers, allies and advantages, and they had them for a long, long while. Their dogma cannot allow for themselves to accept that fact, though. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T02:16:50-08:00","id":409821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408607#post408607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When considering playing the Pure, don't forget their Totems and the crippling restrictions they give the packs they enslave. The Pure book mentions, as examples of totem bans that apply to individual Pure packs, offering their Totem children's fingers every couple days; having to fuck whenever there's a chance, having to consume human or wolf flesh once a week while still keeping their Harmony higher than 5; burning down at least one building per week, etc. Pure totem bans take away a significant part of a werewolf's freedom. That's the price the Pure pay for an existence that is safer and less plagued by moral quandaries and concerns than that of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> (And rest of arguments)</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I <b>despise</b> Pure as antagonists - they are one dimensional. Their portray in 1ed corebook and putting as (semi)central antagonists in book, with putting their as deluded madmans TRIBES made me do not like the game in 1ed line. I even can easier relate to broken Bale Hounds that see only the end of world, than Pure that work with those inhumanity, terror and self-delusion and <i>still</i> think their are &quot;normal&quot;. They are just laying all the time to themselves.<br /> <br /> I'm <b>Mage</b> ST, first and foremost, and Pure looks to me as perverted werewolf version of Seers of Throne - more extreme, more screwed in the head, more bestial. It looks like the gameline want to tell me &quot;instead of lonely psychopath werewolf killing humans, you have 3 Tribes of them&quot;. Especially with those self-destroying Culture of Hate.<br /> <br /> On one hand they try to be bestial and do immoral things. On other, they restrict themselves to milder ways than Bale Hounds - but only in words.<br /> <br /> When with some Seers of Throne I can reason ( I point I do not like the Order as whole ), the Pure are just unreasonable for me, even as antagonists. Because now they are build &quot;let's put madman Tribe A, B or C, even if their inner culture makes them to destroy themselves, if Forsaken are out of sight&quot;. I really need some redeemable features for them, cause now they are only &quot;black and blackness&quot; hunters, not real persons to make great antagonists. They are beasts to slain on sight, nor reason with in any way. There is nothing in their write up to point Forsaken players &quot;they can have right, maybe <i>you</i> are the bad guys here&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong, but good antagonist should make players wonder if they are doing really a good thing, especially in World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-18-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:18:56-08:00","id":409851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409821#post409821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why I <b>despise</b> Pure as antagonists - they are one dimensional.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409821#post409821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, yes. <br /> <br /> I recommend reading the Pure book. It should clear up a lot. I'm not interested in discussing the Pure with you. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:30:32-08:00","id":409854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409821#post409821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm <b>Mage</b> ST, first and foremost, and Pure looks to me as perverted werewolf version of Seers of Throne - more extreme, more screwed in the head, more bestial. It looks like the gameline want to tell me &quot;instead of lonely psychopath werewolf killing humans, you have 3 Tribes of them&quot;. Especially with those self-destroying Culture of Hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're more like the Garou of Werewolf the Apocalypse (most especially the Red Talons and Silver Fangs) but without being painted as noble and right.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T03:45:31-08:00","id":409867,"title":"","content":"On the topic of playing the Pure: <br /> <br /> Short version: not much interested. <br /> <br /> Longer version: I've played a whole lot of bad guys in my function as a storyteller, and enjoyed most of it. As a player, I've played a few pretty &quot;dark&quot; Forsaken characters. There was also this one Bale Hound PC whose main storyline was something like &quot;fall from grace&quot; followed by eventual redemption and sacrifice. All good fun. <br /> <br /> I'm far less interested in playing Pure. <br /> <br /> For one, the Pure don't have that much in the way of interesting antagonists. They're the top dogs, right? Who are they reasonably afraid of? The Forsaken are in a weaker position than the Pure; spirits generally don't mess with them. Far more interesting to play the underdogs. <br /> <br /> Let's also not forget their totems, their culture and the crippling restrictions thereof. Ultra-limiting bans? Frequent rites of purification? A strong chain of command where you get to take orders and do what you're told? There is quite simply less of a range for characters to be played with the Pure. <br /> <br /> The only scenario I could see as being interesting in the context of playing the Pure is exploring the <i>motivations </i>for individual Pure doing what they do - which might be similar to, say, exploring the motivations for ISIS fighters or terrorists. <br /> <br /> Note how this is <i>specifically different</i> from <i>glorifying </i>the ideologies or playing for squick value - I have seen posters on this forum advocate Pure games featuring play styles whose basic message boiled down to &quot;hey those Pure are so much more awesome than the Forsaken!&quot;. I'm not interested in that shit, and, frankly, I'm never going to game with people like that. I find that sort of thing to be disgusting. A Pure game shouldn't be about violence and victimization solely because evil is so awesome. The Pure serve a different role in the setting. If you think that the Pure are better (morally better, that is, or &quot;right&quot;) than the Forsaken, then you're not a person I am interested in spending any time with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T04:16:49-08:00","id":409881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409867#post409867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Note how this is <i>specifically different</i> from <i>glorifying </i>the ideologies or playing for squick value - I have seen posters on this forum advocate Pure games featuring play styles whose basic message boiled down to &quot;hey those Pure are so much more awesome than the Forsaken!&quot;. I'm not interested in that shit, and, frankly, I'm never going to game with people like that. I find that sort of thing to be disgusting. A Pure game shouldn't be about violence and victimization solely because evil is so awesome. The Pure serve a different role in the setting. If you think that the Pure are better (morally better, that is, or &quot;right&quot;) than the Forsaken, then you're not a person I am interested in spending any time with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mh, I think if anyone want to play ''kill, slash, burn, fight'' can easly take back masquerade and play the sabbat.<br /> Playing the pures is an extremly mature game I think, one smart player probably want to play them more because he want to think and understand something about this kind of evil than play just to make some fun.<br /> Because playing the pure could be everything but <u><b>not</b></u> funny.<br /> But I have no problem if anyone at my table prefer the pure to the forsaken just because they are the bad guys. It doesn't mean that he will go out and make the same thing the pure tribes do lol<br /> I know my friends and I play only with Friends. If the villain have no charm, is probably a bad villain. Anyone of us could like any villain in a comic or in a movie, after all ^^<br /> Just keep your head on your shoulders, I mean, it's a game.<br /> Just say goodbye to the zealots who have ONLY rpg in their life, I think this is what you mean, tell me if I am wrong, btw, seriously, there are people who play werewolf and believe in the Pure dogmas? I hope not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T06:39:45-08:00","id":410038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409867#post409867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of playing the Pure:<br /> <br /> Short version: not much interested.<br /> <br /> Longer version: I've played a whole lot of bad guys in my function as a storyteller, and enjoyed most of it. As a player, I've played a few pretty &quot;dark&quot; Forsaken characters. There was also this one Bale Hound PC whose main storyline was something like &quot;fall from grace&quot; followed by eventual redemption and sacrifice. All good fun.<br /> <br /> I'm far less interested in playing Pure.<br /> <br /> For one, the Pure don't have that much in the way of interesting antagonists. They're the top dogs, right? Who are they reasonably afraid of? The Forsaken are in a weaker position than the Pure; spirits generally don't mess with them. Far more interesting to play the underdogs.<br /> <br /> Let's also not forget their totems, their culture and the crippling restrictions thereof. Ultra-limiting bans? Frequent rites of purification? A strong chain of command where you get to take orders and do what you're told? There is quite simply less of a range for characters to be played with the Pure.<br /> <br /> The only scenario I could see as being interesting in the context of playing the Pure is exploring the <i>motivations </i>for individual Pure doing what they do - which might be similar to, say, exploring the motivations for ISIS fighters or terrorists.<br /> <br /> Note how this is <i>specifically different</i> from <i>glorifying </i>the ideologies or playing for squick value - I have seen posters on this forum advocate Pure games featuring play styles whose basic message boiled down to &quot;hey those Pure are so much more awesome than the Forsaken!&quot;. I'm not interested in that shit, and, frankly, I'm never going to game with people like that. I find that sort of thing to be disgusting. A Pure game shouldn't be about violence and victimization solely because evil is so awesome. The Pure serve a different role in the setting. If you think that the Pure are better (morally better, that is, or &quot;right&quot;) than the Forsaken, then you're not a person I am interested in spending any time with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is weird, as you told you do not talk with me about Pure, but say <b>exactly</b> my point on them. At least as 1ed corebook show them - they are self-deluded psychopaths. They do not <b>any</b> good argument to the Forsaken, only brainwashing and serving spirits. Maybe when I read <b>Pure</b> I will get &quot;wider perspective&quot;, but from the tidbits you post here and talk about, it's showing more of the same that core serves - and it's one dimensional antagonists.<br /> <br /> They can work even as Seers, when the Order is Evil, but individual Seers can at least be sympathetic. In Pure there is only Hatred, in three favors,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:05:58-08:00","id":410053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410038#post410038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is weird, as you told you do not talk with me about Pure, but say <b>exactly</b> my point on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you're not reading within context. He's speaking about <i>playing the Pure</i>, while you're saying they're <i>bad antagonists</i>. There is a fundamental difference in 'these are not suitable bad guys' and 'I wouldn't want to play this kind of bad guy'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T07:42:58-08:00","id":410085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410038#post410038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can work even as Seers, when the Order is Evil, but individual Seers can at least be sympathetic. In Pure there is only Hatred, in three favors,</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of that hatred can be borne from ignorance.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible for someone to be in the Pure because they don't know any better. They believe what the Pure say. Maybe they've been a victim of Forsaken brutalities, which are common enough. There's a pack in, I think the anthology but it may have been one of the books, the alpha of which was plotted against by the 'leader' of a protectorate, who essentially sacrificed them to the Pure and smeared the alpha's name. If you were a newly changed pup in that pack and just got sold out by a leader of the Forsaken, you might even see some truth to the Pure's lies.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they do have a 'win condition,' in the re-emergence of Pangaea, either taking the world back to that or changing the current world enough to make it seem like that. I don't believe it's possible either way, but I'm able to look at the books and see a broader picture that characters in the game cannot. The idea of being able to land a solid victory, as opposed to an eternity of endless battle, is probably enough to sway a lot of werewolves. The price may be the death of Forsaken but they were going to die in their unending fight anyways, and they're in the way.<br /> <br /> And of course there's probably at least a few Pure who want to get out, but don't see it as a realistic option. Continuing with the terrorism analogy, there's people who went to join up with these groups because they believe in the cause, but they weren't aware of the realities of the situation, and how they'd be treated in it. But just getting up and leaving isn't really an option once you've joined the Pure. The Lodge of Salvation can theoretically bring you back into Luna's good graces, but how common are they and how likely is a Pure that wants to convert to meet one? And even after that change, they would be marked by the Pure, hunted perhaps forever by people who knew what they did.<br /> <br /> And of course it all depends on the Pure being wrong and the Forsaken being right. Maybe the Forsaken are just deluded pawns of a crazed moon goddess and the only thing in the Pure's way to bringing back Pangaea or Father Wolf. And that's up to the individual Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:06:13-08:00","id":410150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410085#post410085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course there's probably at least a few Pure who want to get out, but don't see it as a realistic option. Continuing with the terrorism analogy, there's people who went to join up with these groups because they believe in the cause, but they weren't aware of the realities of the situation, and how they'd be treated in it. But just getting up and leaving isn't really an option once you've joined the Pure. The Lodge of Salvation can theoretically bring you back into Luna's good graces, but how common are they and how likely is a Pure that wants to convert to meet one? And even after that change, they would be marked by the Pure, hunted perhaps forever by people who knew what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see those character, but they are &quot;broken antagonists&quot;, not working with the &quot;system&quot; the setting proposing - I want something totally diffrent. Lately, on <b>Mage</b> forum, here is talk about sympethetic Seers. There is in there idea of character that knows that Exarchs are reality bastards, and he wants to appese them before they will destroy the world if Pentacle will make big move. Or character that really thinks that controlling magic is a way to make people safe. Those character are very good working with the Seers, and some PCs and players can reason with their goals.<br /> <br /> This contrast with Pure, that totally turn themselves on humanity from which they come and would do not anything to save them - how players can reason with that? Those things just sell they race without even good motivation.<br /> <br /> They are made &quot;beasts with brains, but still lesser than Bale Hounds&quot;. They niche in the setting is to be random foot soldier/beast rampaging the territory of PCs - not in any way character you can reason with, talk with. They just want you dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410085#post410085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course it all depends on the Pure being wrong and the Forsaken being right. Maybe the Forsaken are just deluded pawns of a crazed moon goddess and the only thing in the Pure's way to bringing back Pangaea or Father Wolf. And that's up to the individual Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rising Pangaea maybe a good thing? In any instance? HOW, I ask?<br /> <br /> Seeing what spirits for now, how they treat both humanity <b>and</b> Uratha how can anyone would work for them? They just want to make everyone their slaves. At least Exarchs are promoting those that works for them. When spirits will be infuancing the Flesh openly, we will return to Stone Age.<br /> <br /> I can get Bale Hounds, as they are shown as totally broken souls, but Pure need arguments for they idealogy - something that makes sens for their goal and brutality. And not the &quot;Wolfs Slaing Myth&quot;, as there at least <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths\">few variants of them</a> in 2ed.<br /> <br /> To make reasonalbe character, Pure pups should see <b>now</b> they can have right. Not to avange long dead spirit god, but that their actions do something &quot;good&quot; to the world - or at least humans they care for. The problem is I really cannot see them that way - only as deluded psychopaths. Forsaken bring balance to the world of Flesh and Spirit. Seers make magic restricted, but also not destroying the world. Pure do not do both of this things - they just want to burn the world in battle where Forsaken are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-18-2015, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:38:16-08:00","id":410209,"title":"","content":"No point in discussing this sort of thing with him. I would prefer for this thread to move into a more productive direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:55:58-08:00","id":410254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=409764#post409764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember, also, that the Pure truly believe themselves to be victims of a cosmic struggle that started an apocalypse ago. They whine about being martyrs for a holy cause, they think they're the underdogs of the setting who've been wronged more than anyone else - yet they have all the numbers, allies and advantages, and they had them for a long, long while. Their dogma cannot allow for themselves to accept that fact, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true, though. The books are very explicit that their numbers wax and wane. They are currently at a high point because they took advantage of the Brethren Wars in the 80s and 90s and claimed a lot of territory. Prior to that, though, they were explicitly lurking in the margins with territories in isolated places. And this has been the pattern. While they have their advantages, they don't have all the advantages. Their totems are more powerful and they get along better with spirits, but the Forsaken have Luna on their side, less susceptibility to silver and aren't operating under the crippling bans the Pure are, from both their pack and tribal totems. As for numbers, the Pure are often self-limiting. The Fire-Touched rituals are so abusive that they must have a high mortality rate (many of them set their new recruits on fire, for God's sake). Ivory Claws are incredibly picky in who they will take, refusing to even consider someone who Luna even smiled at. Predator Kings live a lifestyle of incredible violence, even for werewolves, and their problem with human artifacts drives them into the boonies, away from resources and breeding stock. Their culture of paranoia and constant competition to prove themselves Purer-than-thou would lead to a lot of packs imploding, like many extreme religious cults.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:06:01-08:00","id":410268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410150#post410150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rising Pangaea maybe a good thing? In any instance? HOW, I ask?<br /> <br /> Seeing what spirits for now, how they treat both humanity <b>and</b> Uratha how can anyone would work for them? They just want to make everyone their slaves. At least Exarchs are promoting those that works for them. When spirits will be infuancing the Flesh openly, we will return to Stone Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bad thing for us, with the end of our civilization, but it's great for the Predator Kings, who want to go back to the stone age. The Pure enslave themselves to totems because they need power and big guns for their war, but if the war is over they no longer need to do that.<br /> <br /> It's the reasoning behind almost every war. They think things will be better for them when they win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:49:43-08:00","id":410320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410254#post410254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't true, though. The books are very explicit that their numbers wax and wane.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet, globally, the Pure have nearly twice the numbers of the Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T10:53:41-08:00","id":410325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410320#post410320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet, globally, the Pure have nearly twice the numbers of the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is in present day Werewolf, we're living after the Brethren Wars, where so many of the Forsaken were killed through in-fighting and Pure attacks. The Forsaken are still rebuilding their numbers and the Pure have a lot of new recruits from all the wolf-blooded and converts they captured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:38:01-08:00","id":410379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410268#post410268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a bad thing for us, with the end of our civilization, but it's great for the Predator Kings, who want to go back to the stone age. The Pure enslave themselves to totems because they need power and big guns for their war, but if the war is over they no longer need to do that.<br /> <br /> It's the reasoning behind almost every war. They think things will be better for them when they win.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is somewhat logical for Predator Kings, but Ivory Claws and Fire-Touched do not, in truth, regain things with return of Pangea. Without Forsaken cultivatings Father Wolf work of balancing the Flesh and Spirit, the Spirit will gone wild, overtake humanity and even <b>more</b> will be jaded on Uratha. Then both Claws and Touched would not rule the spirits and humans, only make a great mess - because Predatory Kings &quot;need&quot; their big beast to hunt.<br /> <br /> This alliance is illogical, especially, as the &quot;War&quot; with Forsaken lasts as long as human history, No one could be so deluded to think that &quot;win is night!&quot; after all those millenia... It's like saying that &quot;Hieromagus will be today!&quot; in <b>Mage</b> - and that three Orders would firmly believe in that.<br /> <br /> Return of Pangea will not lend any profits for werewolves race, open war with Forsaken is only working for one of three Tribes ( the Predator Kings ), and Pure could not say they are descendants of Father Wolf if they forsake ( pun not intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) his duties in times of Pangea. This is why I think their are deluded - they &quot;rations&quot; do not hold up, even slightness.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the <b>Pure</b> book mentions things that change those problems I pointed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T11:44:53-08:00","id":410384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410379#post410379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This alliance is illogical, especially, as the &quot;War&quot; with Forsaken lasts as long as human history, No one could be so deluded to think that &quot;win is night!&quot; after all those millenia... It's like saying that &quot;Hieromagus will be today!&quot; in <b>Mage</b> - and that three Orders would firmly believe in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are people in real life who are right now fighting a war that was started over a thousand years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Return of Pangea will not lend any profits for werewolves race, open war with Forsaken is only working for one of three Tribes ( the Predator Kings ), and Pure could not say they are descendants of Father Wolf if they forsake ( pun not intended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) his duties in times of Pangea. This is why I think their are deluded - they &quot;rations&quot; do not hold up, even slightness.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the <b>Pure</b> book mentions things that change those problems I pointed? </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, you should probably read the book if you want to know more about the Pure side of things. The core book barely scratches the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:08:32-08:00","id":410416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410384#post410384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are people in real life who are right now fighting a war that was started over a thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Who are they? I ask genuinely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410384#post410384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you should probably read the book if you want to know more about the Pure side of things. The core book barely scratches the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask nicely so you can answer my question - I do not plan to read the whole supplement on idea that I think is poorly done, uninteresting in long play, and just bad for the game for now. But if you point me there are answers to the problems I mentioned ( and not only more of &quot;Pure must kill Forsaken, because their hate them&quot;, but real answers to the problems I pointed ), I will gladly dwell in to them.<br /> <br /> You know - I really want to like idea of Pure, because it's just one of main points of <b>Werewolf</b> setting. But as pictured in corebook - I can't, and do not want to touch that a 8 foot pole with. It's just &quot;terrorist fanatics with no real base&quot; kind a thing.<br /> <br /> For example, I could understand that Pure believes Forsaken betrayed the Wolf for the Moon, and that they are not worthy of calling themselves the children of first one. They would then try to dominate all the spirits, calling it's their sacred duty to govern the Shadow Realm and that the Uratha should rule the returning Pangea - this idea I could support.<br /> <br /> But the 1ed corebook describing them as slaves to the spirits - they should rule on them by the mandate of Wolf - and they work for the spirits they should dominate. Also, from the picturing of Pangea in book, it will look like nightmare for any one that is not the spirit - Hisil will just overwhelm the Earth, leaving everyone lose - beside spirit lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:15:12-08:00","id":410424,"title":"","content":"Debating numbers is negligible, bale hounds are supposed to be an extreme minority yet in wod uk the bale hounds grossly outnumber the pure and forsaken. Hell they have full on packs owning the country side!<br /> <br /> at any rate they're all correct, the pure outnumber the forsaken by a pretty sizable lead. There are a few regretting their life choices. I can't recall which book it is, but there's an old predator king who is contemplating his life, and his story hook involves converting him back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:29:47-08:00","id":410438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410416#post410416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Who are they? I ask genuinely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The aforementioned ISIS.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask nicely so you can answer my question - I do not plan to read the whole supplement on idea that I think is poorly done, uninteresting in long play, and just bad for the game for now. But if you point me there are answers to the problems I mentioned ( and not only more of &quot;Pure must kill Forsaken, because their hate them&quot;, but real answers to the problems I pointed ), I will gladly dwell in to them. </div> </div> </div>Then don't worry about it. There's a whole book that goes into the depths of the Pure beliefs, from resurrecting Father Wolf to Taga Dan, the Fire-Touched version of heaven. But nothing's wrong with running them as psychopaths or just using what little the core book says of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-18-2015, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:43:40-08:00","id":410445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=408579#post408579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right, there's probably a lodge or two with some concept of an afterlife as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Points to Lodge of the Savior*<br /> <br /> Anyway, for reasons I can't really explain, this thread has made me interested in maybe writing up some &quot;Mirror Mirror&quot;-y type Pure Tribes; that is, reimagining the Pure Tribes through the less &quot;Anthrophobic&quot;(for lack of a better phrase) worldview of the Forsaken for use if someone were to play some sort of AU game or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:45:00-08:00","id":410446,"title":"","content":"But does <b>Pure</b> book answer my concerns with logical side of resurrecting Pangea or that the Pure serve the spirits, when they should rule them? Is all those things make sense from the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T12:50:24-08:00","id":410450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410446#post410446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does <b>Pure</b> book answer my concerns with logical side of resurrecting Pangea or that the Pure serve the spirits, when they should rule them? Is all those things make sense from the book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Though if by logical side of resurrecting Pangaea you mean exactly how it's done, there is no set method. Some believe it can be done by killing or converting all the Forsaken, some by letting the Beshilu gnaw away the Gauntlet, and some just empower the Shadow. Some accept that Pangaea is gone, but the glories of that age can be reclaimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:00:43-08:00","id":410456,"title":"","content":"&quot;By logical side of resurrecting Pangaea&quot; I meant the merits they see in it. Because from the build of the setting now, it would only end in both human <b>and</b> werewolves enslavement by the spirits. <i>Hisil</i> is more numerous, powerful and united than Uratha will be. The Pure could not think they can control it in reality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:03:47-08:00","id":410460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410456#post410456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;By logical side of resurrecting Pangaea&quot; I meant the merits they see in it. Because from the build of the setting now, it would only end in both human <b>and</b> werewolves enslavement by the spirits. <i>Hisil</i> is more numerous, powerful and united than Uratha will be. The Pure could not think they can control it in reality...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then still yes, and they believe they will be the top predators, like they were meant to be. To them, the Forsaken are slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:17:32-08:00","id":410492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410456#post410456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;By logical side of resurrecting Pangaea&quot; I meant the merits they see in it. Because from the build of the setting now, it would only end in both human <b>and</b> werewolves enslavement by the spirits. <i>Hisil</i> is more numerous, powerful and united than Uratha will be. The Pure could not think they can control it in reality...</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost all political philosophies have an untenable endpoint. The religions seek to create &quot;heaven on earth&quot;, the Marxists want to create a perfect classless society, etc. The fact that the endpoint is unobtainable isn't the driving forces behind these but rather existing grievances with the current state of affairs and a desire to either put things back to the way they were or reform the system so that they will be able to enjoy the desires that they want.<br /> <br /> The Pure, for the most part, are either blinded by their hate and/or simply rationalize the end state of the world in which that if they managed to bring back &quot;Panegaea&quot;, they will be in a much better place than they currently are now.<br /> <br /> Kinda reminds me a lot of a few of the Movements among the Deceived once you think about it...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T13:49:01-08:00","id":410509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410460#post410460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then still yes, and they believe they will be the top predators, like they were meant to be. To them, the Forsaken are slaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting - how so? It's the Pure that makes every spirits biding. Yes, Forsaken works for Moon/Luna, but it's very distant relation. The Pure makes human sacrifices or bloody rituals every other day for <b>their</b> spiritual masters ( once again, the corebook point of view ).<br /> <br /> I really never get why just Pure demand the respect in the spirits - it's Forsaken that goes with this &quot;caustious ecology of Flesh and Spirit&quot;. Pure just should proclaim and sustain their rightful place at top of food chain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T14:00:17-08:00","id":410519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410509#post410509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting - how so? It's the Pure that makes every spirits biding. Yes, Forsaken works for Moon/Luna, but it's very distant relation. The Pure makes human sacrifices or bloody rituals every other day for <b>their</b> spiritual masters ( once again, the corebook point of view ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the core book say that? The Pure book really paints them differently, but the core book was always sparse on the details. There's not enough people in the world for the Pure to sacrifice them every day. About Luna being a 'distant relation,' the Forsaken are bound by the Oaths of the Moon and the silver brands of Renown, which the Pure see as chains the Forsaken willingly bind themselves in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really never get why just Pure demand the respect in the spirits - it's Forsaken that goes with this &quot;caustious ecology of Flesh and Spirit&quot;. Pure just should proclaim and sustain their rightful place at top of food chain. </div> </div> </div>Spirits are naturally more agreeable with the Pure because they both want the same thing. The Forsaken are the ones holding up the Gauntlet and keeping the sides from mixing. The Pure want really powerful totems, and this is where they screw themselves over, because the spirits they bind as totems are more often than not too powerful to work on the level that Forsaken totems do. They give the pack great powers in return, and can command spirits because of their rank. As someone noted before, however, they demand a steep price to keep up that power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-18-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:35:03-08:00","id":410728,"title":"","content":"Man, I could write a whole load about why Pure are great antagonists but it's a bit late here at the moment for me to plunge into it.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say that, quite the opposite of being one-dimensional, I sometimes find the Pure to have too many dimensions and have to slim them down and focus them on just some of their dimensions to make them more compelling villains for the given chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T16:37:01-08:00","id":410730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410325#post410325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is in present day Werewolf, we're living after the Brethren Wars, where so many of the Forsaken were killed through in-fighting and Pure attacks. The Forsaken are still rebuilding their numbers and the Pure have a lot of new recruits from all the wolf-blooded and converts they captured.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure page 16<br /> <br /> &quot;The Pure, in most areas, outnumber the Forsaken&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pure page 83<br /> <br /> &quot;The Pure Tribes outnumber the Forsaken by nearly two to one.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pure page 166<br /> <br /> &quot;This region is a microcosm for the Pure versus Forsaken conflict <i>the world over</i> \u2014 the Pure are ascendant and the Forsaken fight for their lives against<i> superior numbers </i>and hate-driven enemies who have cast aside their ties to Luna.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of these statements include the qualifier &quot;in North America.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T17:56:50-08:00","id":410857,"title":"","content":"Someone should have written how the clash between the Silver Syndicate and Howl Before Time went in the anthology tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:30:11-08:00","id":410881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410730#post410730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Pure page 16<br /> <br /> &quot;The Pure, in most areas, outnumber the Forsaken&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pure page 83<br /> <br /> &quot;The Pure Tribes outnumber the Forsaken by nearly two to one.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pure page 166<br /> <br /> &quot;This region is a microcosm for the Pure versus Forsaken conflict <i>the world over</i> \u2014 the Pure are ascendant and the Forsaken fight for their lives against<i> superior numbers </i>and hate-driven enemies who have cast aside their ties to Luna.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of these statements include the qualifier &quot;in North America.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure are explicitly outnumbered by the Forsaken in the United Kingdom, but hold superior territories through terror tactics and persistent bluffing. This is described in Shadows of the United Kingdom.<br /> <br /> So it's certainly not universal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T18:44:20-08:00","id":410890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410730#post410730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of these statements include the qualifier &quot;in North America.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things, first on page 14.<br /> <br /> 'The Pure\u2019s numbers have not always remained strong. The centuries have seen the imbalance between the Forsaken and the Pure shift again and again.<br /> The general rule seems to be this: in times and places of trouble, the Pure numbers dwindle.'<br /> <br /> That's the setting of the game. Pure numbers are strong, and it is a time of trouble.<br /> <br /> The second is that while the Pure book suggests the Brethren War only occurred in North America, the core and other books suggest it was a global thing, and the write-up for the Lodge of Unity says it happened in North and South America.<br /> <br /> This is kind of derailing though, so in the interests of heading that off, obviously the Pure have numerical advantage right now, but they don't always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-18-2015, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:23:12-08:00","id":411123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=410509#post410509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure just should proclaim and sustain their rightful place at top of food chain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha ha ha ha ha ha haaaaaaa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *wipes tear*<br /> <br /> Oh, you were serious?<br /> <br /> Werewolves have never been top of the food chain. So many spirits are bigger than they are. So many spirits could murder and eat them. Even back in the days of Father Wolf, when they killed the top predator, they quickly sought protection and guidance from bigger spirits. Werewolves have strength in numbers, and pack tactics, and human ingenuity to give them the competitive edge. At best they're co-leaders in the food chain, but many, many spirits can eat them too.<br /> <br /> Now, Forsaken understand that they should be dominant. They murdered Urfarah, they should take his place of dominance, but also his duties that come with it. They understand they need allies and patronage. They have tribes, they have lodges, and on a pack level, they have totem spirits they can manage and dominate.<br /> <br /> Pure don't get that. They just want dominance without duty, and they haven't earned either. They didn't claim their place as top dog (pun intended), and they panicked. The Forsaken were on top and that scared the Pure. They didn't consider that Father Wolf kept the bigger spirits controlled, all they saw was the power and protection of bigger spirits, to give them breathing room to beat the Forsaken. They signed up to poor, lopsided bargains - more power for unreasonable demands. The spirits don't care if they burn the Pure out - more puppet servants where they came from. The Pure can't break the cycle because the spirits have a vested interest in keeping werewolves subjugated. Look what happened last time they came together as one. <br /> <br /> The Pure all have reasons for what they believe and do, but at heart their culture is built on a foundation of cowardice and subservience. Their numbers may be greater because of their spirit masters, but does victory as a slave really count as victory?<br /> <br /> Just one possible view of the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:57:10-08:00","id":412403,"title":"","content":"First, <b>Bunyip</b>, thanks for awesome take on Pure - they changed from &quot;immoral fanatics&quot; to &quot;lazy sellouts&quot;. Still, I want to find some positive things with them - like you could realate at least in part with Seers of Throne in <b>Mage</b>. I really, really would like to connect to them, at least in part as ST, to better could sell them on game sessions. Cause they still sound to me as &quot;stupid/self-denialed/etc&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I ending first chapter of <b>Pure</b> book, so I see all the ideas you mentioned before - still, the answer on antagonists is mostly the same - hate crime psychopats. I want genuine &quot;persons&quot;, that are not totally unhinged by the hate only.<br /> <br /> P.S. Loving the use of polish word &quot;Pogrom&quot; in context of first near-annihilation of Pure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=411123#post411123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves have never been top of the food chain. So many spirits are bigger than they are. So many spirits could murder and eat them. Even back in the days of Father Wolf, when they killed the top predator, they quickly sought protection and guidance from bigger spirits. Werewolves have strength in numbers, and pack tactics, and human ingenuity to give them the competitive edge. At best they're co-leaders in the food chain, but many, many spirits can eat them too.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it was obvious on begining of the topic. But then I thought that Urfarah is so central being for the Pure, they could want to reclaim that. With your pointing how Pangea was clearly nothing to return to with ( spirits still will trump Uratha ), why Pure are so fixated on this? Or, other way, around - what they could &quot;good&quot; it would bring to the world for werewolves as a whole? And I do not want to get here Predator Kings stand &quot;we will have things to hunt&quot;, but real, genuine answer - what could Pure elders point to pups and said &quot;and with new Pangea it will be good, for our race&quot;. Because now, at least if you are not Predator Kings psycho, you will see that Pangea will be devastating for your own kind if you think about it - spirits and flesh merging, Spirits Lords on top even more than now. How, beside the PK hunt fanatics, would want that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=411123#post411123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure don't get that. They just want dominance without duty, and they haven't earned either. They didn't claim their place as top dog (pun intended), and they panicked. The Forsaken were on top and that scared the Pure. They didn't consider that Father Wolf kept the bigger spirits controlled, all they saw was the power and protection of bigger spirits, to give them breathing room to beat the Forsaken. They signed up to poor, lopsided bargains - more power for unreasonable demands. The spirits don't care if they burn the Pure out - more puppet servants where they came from. The Pure can't break the cycle because the spirits have a vested interest in keeping werewolves subjugated. Look what happened last time they came together as one.<br /> <br /> The Pure all have reasons for what they believe and do, but at heart their culture is built on a foundation of cowardice and subservience. Their numbers may be greater because of their spirit masters, but does victory as a slave really count as victory?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the way I have most problem with - Pure are, well... pure. They paint themselves as morally higher than Forsaken. They gone with alliance with spirits for survival reasons - I can relate to those, okay. But when I read they worship they Totems, adore them, fixate on them, only because of long lasting alliance I say &quot;what?!&quot; - Pure worship Father Wolf. They have obsession on him ( like Forsaken have on Luna ), they want his respect. I can get they want to &quot;steal it&quot;, so they struck the bargains with spirits - dark and mighty. But open slavery? That the Bale Hounds reasons are for in setting.<br /> <br /> I could support Pure stance as &quot;we have powerful alliance (spirits) and must do some nasty things to sustain this agreement&quot; - yes. But not worship. Not dedication, not in hearts. Pure should use as much Spirits Lords, as Spirit Lords use Pure. Agreement of convenience, than of slavery. Maybe it is century old deal, but there should be times the Pure pack overthrow their Totem if they think it gone to far, even for them. Because Pure are werewolves also, and being spirits pushover is not going in Father Wolf footsteps.<br /> <br /> As to 2ed things, I have some questions to the Pure and their numbers in context of changes.<br /> <br /> 1. In 2ed both Forsaken and Pure <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forsaken-saturday/\" target=\"_blank\">Packs are cults, families, gangs and other tightly related organisations</a> - with werewolves being center of the group, but rest of members being &quot;in the fold/in family&quot;. I imagine that this makes any Wolf-Blooded or near-Change humans being resource for future Uratha in those groups. The <b>Pure</b> points this is one of main reasons why those Tribes have greater numbers - they &quot;breed&quot; their future members in the groups like that. But in 2ed I imagine Forsaken do the same, all the time. Does this &quot;one greater advantage&quot;, now splintered on boths factions, get with in Forsaken favor. Especially as running 2ed Pack of Pure from multi-tribes is practically impossible, seeing how, for example, Predator Kings are diffrent from Fire-Touched. Does it all makes &quot;Pure are stronger in numbers&quot; thing less plausible?<br /> <br /> 2. With 2ed Harmony rules I assume most Pure are going quickly for the Spirit end of spectrum. But to stop this, the need <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forsaken-saturday/\" target=\"_blank\">Touchstones</a> that will bring them more in line to the Man side, So maybe we will see more &quot;human&quot; side of Pure, when they are &quot;killer Predator King by night, loyal and dedicated father to his daughter by day&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-20-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T21:39:59-08:00","id":412420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/407873-the-way-you-play-the-pure-tribes?p=411123#post411123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha ha ha ha ha ha haaaaaaa <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *wipes tear*<br /> <br /> Oh, you were serious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the wyrdhamster zone. Other star attractions include &quot;why aren't the beings who are metaphysically burning at all times more enthusiastic about how awesome being on fire is?&quot; and &quot;demonic Agendas are one-dimensional universal character traits because I say so.&quot; We hope to see our latest addition, &quot;Can't my cultish anti-human hate-criminal be sympathetic and playable in a way that precludes being a cultish anti-human hate-criminal?&quot; produce a fresh new crop of Got-It-Wrongite by the second fiscal quarter, because the machine-elves that set our operating budget gave us a quota and if we don't meet projections they poke us with sticks.<br /> <br /> Please send ointment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T00:16:22-08:00","id":412497,"title":"","content":"Don't forget &quot;Modern Japan should move to the whims of Feudal Japan&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T08:58:24-08:00","id":412857,"title":"","content":"And what about the War guys?<br /> How do you portrait it?<br /> I don't think that those questions could be off-topic. After all, if you are the storyteller, you <i>have </i>to play the pure as antagonists so...<br /> Do you try to kill the forsaken on sight?<br /> Do you prefer the dominace-territory fight?<br /> Remember that killing an uratha, both forsaken or pure, could be very dangerous, for Harmony and territory relationship....<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer the dominance-territory fight. I don't see logic in a ''killing spree'' fight between forsaken and pure for a lot of reasons.<br /> Number one, killing werewolves are dangerous for both Anshega and Uratha for a matter of harmony and so on.<br /> Number two, it's not a matter of whole confederation of uratha ( like the old Apocalypse, where you share the sept with a lot of members), it's a matter of packs.<br /> Every pack have different goals, in a way or another. And territorial problems and rivalities are among the pure as the forsaken. Sometimes, new players have problems understanding it, they think about a large-scale war where forsaken and pure slaughter themselves any time they see one another.<br /> Not less important, the renown.<br /> Personally, a pure killing a forsaken during a large scale conflict between packs it's different than a pure killing a forsaken just because he find the right chance ( stab him, cut his throat, take advantage of a possible situation, maybe just on a territorial brawl).<br /> Of course every tribes it's different on this. The Ivory Claws maybe, despite their hatred and more sopisticated war-tactics, could be the tribe more inclined to honorable ritual challenge, maybe to death, maybe not to subtract a part of forsakne territory.<br /> Some Fire Touched maybe only prefer a social war, trying to manipulate the forsaken and some spirits alike.<br /> Maybe the Predator Kings couldn't care less, but for sure they know that premeditate homicides are something bad for their armony (maybe..).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:55:08-08:00","id":412975,"title":"","content":"Harmony isn't as much an issue as it used to be. I think I'd keep it down to terrorist gorilla cell style pack battles for turf. Maybe one giant chronicle to end some massive pure spirit beast","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T12:55:52-08:00","id":413046,"title":"","content":"Those Gorillas are brutal, especially if they are capable of shapeshifting too; doubly so if they are Terrorist Gorillas. . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}